    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Only two registers answer: 40001 (relay outputs) and 40002 (digital inputs). Querying any other register gives an error.",
    "Relay outputs and inputs are one bit each: bit 0 is relay 1 or input 1, up to bit 7 for relay 8 or input 8.",
    "Settings are made with the DIP switches on the front panel with the unit powered off: DIP 1-4 node number 1 to 15, DIP 5 relay hold (OFF = outputs released after 3 minutes without a query, ON = they stay), DIP 6 protocol (OFF Modbus ASCII, ON RTU), DIP 7 framing (OFF 8N1, ON 7E1), DIP 8 speed (OFF 9600, ON 19200). Restart the unit after a change.",
    "Both the ASCII and RTU modes are possible; the RTU 9600 8N1 settings are shown here.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual (in Spanish); not tested on a device."
  ],
